mallocng: representable object bounds for the virtual profile (option iii)

Seven size-class strides raised by 1-4 units each so that every large class's stride is a
multiple of its own bounds granule, and enframe placing each object on a granule-aligned
base. Without both, the compressed encoder truncates an unaligned base DOWNWARD and the
object gains authority below itself; measured against the RTL bounds model, 1497 of 6060
(class, request, slot, cycle) cases decode wrong without this and 0 with it, once the
group header is granule-sized as well.

size_to_class and the slot/class selection are untouched: the request is rounded in the
runtime's own malloc wrapper (runtime/virtual/heap.c), outside musl, so mallocng's
set_size records exactly what the capability covers. check-mallocng-policy.py pins these
seven entries and their values and still refuses any other difference.

